# UPDATED: 2026-10-30
# DOMAIN-SUFFIX: 8
# DOMAIN: 2
# TOTAL: 10
# NOTE: Loon remote-rule format. Policy is set in Loon's Remote Rule entry, not in this file.
# NOTE: Place this rule ABOVE the gmail.com -> static residential rule, otherwise imap.gmail.com will match gmail.com suffix first and stay on IPRoyal chain.
# NOTE: Place this rule BELOW ad-blocking REJECT rules, so amplitude/appsflyer analytics stay REJECT.
# NOTE: imap/smtp are DOMAIN (not suffix) on purpose - only those two Gmail subdomains go to the auto group, other gmail.com traffic stays on static residential.
# Original 5 (blackmatrix7, UPDATED 2025-06-06):
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,amplitude.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,firebaseio.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,hockeyapp.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,readdle.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,smartmailcloud.com
# Spark site / app domains (certificate SAN + app):
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,sparkmailapp.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,sparkmail.app
# Spark push (from Loon log: sdk.fra-01.braze.eu):
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,braze.eu
# Gmail IMAP/SMTP for Spark adding mailbox (from Loon log: imap.gmail.com:993 timed out via IPRoyal HTTP/SOCKS5 chain, 0B download):
DOMAIN,imap.gmail.com
DOMAIN,smtp.gmail.com
